    <string name="send_retry">重试</string>
    <!--
      Why a transfer stopped, in words that name something the user can act on. The
      transport's own wording ("isConnected failed: ECONNREFUSED (Connection refused)")
      is accurate and tells the person holding the phone nothing. Each of these names
      the one thing that has to change on the other device.
    -->
    <!--
      "Refused" is a closed port, and a closed port is not the same claim as "the other
      person turned AirDrop off": a receiver that is asleep, rebuilding its service, or
      simply holding a stale row also refuses. This device reported the old wording while
      the other phone's AirDrop sheet was demonstrably open, so the line now says what is
      true — nothing came back — and asks for the one thing that fixes it.
    -->
    <string name="send_why_refused">对方暂时没有接收，请确认对方 AirDrop 面板开着，稍后重试</string>
    <string name="send_why_reset">连接被对方中断了，请确认对方没有点「拒绝」，并在面板还开着时重试</string>
    <string name="send_why_timeout">对方一直没有回应，请确认对方屏幕亮着、AirDrop 面板开着</string>
    <string name="send_why_unreachable">到对方的链路还没建立起来，请稍等片刻再重试</string>
</resources>
